# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SWAP POINT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "mock"     -> cookie-backed demo data, no database required (default)
# "supabase" -> real Postgres + Supabase Auth
#
# This is the only variable that decides which data provider the app uses.
# It is intentionally NOT prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_: every data call happens in a
# Server Component or Server Action, so neither implementation is ever bundled
# into client-side JavaScript.
DATA_SOURCE=mock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mock mode
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signs the demo-state cookie so it cannot be hand-edited in devtools.
# Mock mode is a demo fixture, NOT a security boundary — see
# src/lib/data/mock/store.ts. Any random string works locally.
MOCK_SECRET=dev-only-change-me

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase mode (only needed when DATA_SOURCE=supabase)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The anon key is safe to expose to the browser; RLS is what protects the data.
# NEVER put the service_role key in this file or anywhere in the app — it
# bypasses RLS entirely. Staff use it only via the Supabase dashboard.
#
# LOCAL (npm run db:start)
#   The URL is always the one below. Copy the anon key from `npm run db:status`
#   — it is generated per machine, so it is deliberately not written here.
#   Local Supabase has "Confirm email" OFF, so sign-up works immediately.
#
# HOSTED
#   Project Settings -> API in the Supabase dashboard. Note that a hosted
#   project has "Confirm email" ON by default, so a new account cannot sign in
#   until the address is confirmed — see the note in supabase/migrations.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
